.TH ZERODDS-MQTT-BRIDGED 1 "" "ZeroDDS" "ZeroDDS Manual"
.SH NAME
zerodds-mqtt-bridged \- DDS to MQTT 5 bridge daemon
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B zerodds-mqtt-bridged
[\fB\-\-config\fR \fIFILE\fR]
[\fB\-\-broker\fR \fIURL\fR]
[\fB\-\-domain\fR \fIID\fR]
[\fB\-\-topic\fR \fIDDS:MQTT\fR]...
[\fB\-\-log\-level\fR \fILEVEL\fR]
[\fB\-V\fR | \fB\-h\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B zerodds-mqtt-bridged
mirrors DDS topics to MQTT 5 broker topics and vice versa. Implements
.IR docs/specs/zerodds-mqtt-bridge-1.0.md .
Talks to any MQTT 5 broker (Mosquitto, EMQX, HiveMQ) over TCP/TLS,
auto-reconnects with exponential back-off, supports per-route MQTT QoS
(0/1/2), Retain, MessageExpiry, ContentType and UserProperties.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-\-config =\fIFILE\fR
The config file (YAML), with drop-ins in its sibling
.IR FILE .d/.
Without it the system file is read when it exists:
.I /etc/zerodds/mqtt-bridged.yaml
with
.I /etc/zerodds/mqtt-bridged.d/
(on macOS under
.IR /usr/local/etc/zerodds );
without that file the built-in defaults apply.
See
.BR zerodds-mqtt-bridged.yaml (5).
.TP
.BR \-\-broker =\fIURL\fR
MQTT broker URL
.RI ( mqtt:// ", " mqtts:// ", " ws:// ", " wss:// ).
.TP
.BR \-\-client\-id =\fIID\fR
MQTT client ID.
.TP
.BR \-\-domain =\fIID\fR
DDS domain ID. Default: 0.
.TP
.BR \-\-username =\fIUSER\fR
MQTT username.
.TP
.BR \-\-password =\fIPASS\fR
MQTT password.
.TP
.BR \-\-tls\-ca =\fIFILE\fR
CA cert.
.TP
.BR \-\-tls\-cert =\fIFILE\fR
Client cert.
.TP
.BR \-\-tls\-key =\fIFILE\fR
Client key.
.TP
.BR \-\-topic =\fIDDS:MQTT\fR
Topic override (repeatable).
.TP
.BR \-\-log\-level =\fILEVEL\fR
Override log level. One of
.IR trace ", " debug ", " info ", " warn ", " error .
.TP
.BR \-\-metrics =\fIADDR\fR
Prometheus listen addr.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Version info.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show the option synopsis.
.TP
.BR \-\-set " \fIPATH\fR=\fIVALUE\fR"
One setting above every file, repeatable;
.BI + PATH = VALUE
appends to a list.
.TP
.B \-\-check\-config
Validate and print the effective configuration with the origin of every
value, then exit: 0 valid, 1 invalid value or unknown key, 2 unreadable
file, syntax error or include cycle.
.SH SIGNALS
.B SIGTERM
graceful shutdown,
.B SIGHUP
reads the configuration again: the topic ACL applies from then on, a
withdrawn read right stops the samples of that topic at once; sessions
persist. Changed topics, broker address or client id, broker TLS, auth mode
or domain need a restart and are logged. A configuration that does not load
changes nothing.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT
Optional OTLP endpoint, such as http://localhost:4318.
.TP
.B MQTT_PASSWORD
The broker password; the setting
.BR mqtt.password ,
above the files, below
.BR \-\-set .
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Normal shutdown (SIGTERM/SIGINT).
.TP
.B 1
Configuration error.
.TP
.B 2
Broker connect error.
.TP
.B 3
DDS discovery error.
.TP
.B 4
TLS error.
.TP
.B 5
Authentication error.
.SH FILES
.I /etc/zerodds/mqtt-bridged.yaml ", " /var/log/zerodds/mqtt-bridged.log .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR zerodds-mqtt-bridged.yaml (5),
.BR mosquitto (8).
.SH STANDARDS
MQTT v5 (OASIS), DDS 1.4, RTPS 2.5.
.SH AUTHORS
ZeroDDS Contributors <release@zerodds.org>.
